<title>UK: Pilkington gets 6.0 mln stg German contract.</title>
<headline>Pilkington gets 6.0 mln stg German contract.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>British glassmaker Pilkington Plc said on Tuesday it received a 6.0 million stg contract to build a solar roof installation for a government building in Herne, Germany.</p>
<p>The 1.0 megawatt roof system for the government training academy would supply up to 900,000 kilowatt hours of solar-produced electricity a year.</p>
<p>Financing will be provided by the local Nordrhein-Westfalen government and the Herne power station, Pilkington said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
